  "guid": "net.drexira.hitmarker",
  "name": "Dragon Den - Hitmarker",
  "slug": "dragon-den-hitmarker",
  "teaser": "Adds hitmarkers, headshot markers, kill markers, damage numbers, and hit sounds. Fully configurable in color, size, fade time, and style.",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/2Hw3v1M4Td1DKkz3bK8Wkzh0MJYFvKTWYXVCi6c6.png",
  "downloads": 19315,
  "favourites_count": 24,
  "description": "<div class=\"tabset\"><div id=\"tabset-1-panel-1\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Features and Usage</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Features</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fully customizable hitmarkers for normal hits, headshots, and kills</li>\n<li>Choose between Cross, X, or custom PNG images for each hit type</li>\n<li>Separate colors for normal, headshot, armor, and kill markers</li>\n<li>Adjustable size, opacity, and fade-out time</li>\n<li>Optional pulse effect on headshots</li>\n<li>Floating damage numbers with rise and fade animations</li>\n<li>Configurable text templates using tokens: {flesh}, {armor} and {bp}</li>\n<li>Choose where damage numbers appear: hit position or screen center</li>\n<li>Optional background behind damage numbers for better visibility</li>\n<li>Detects and colors armor hits, ricochets, and blocked shots</li>\n<li>Plays separate hit and kill sounds with individual volume and file settings</li>\n<li>Master volume control and automatic reload when changing sound files</li>\n<li>Customizable lifetime for hitmarkers and numbers</li>\n<li>Debug mode logs hits, body parts, and weapon info to BepInEx console</li>\n<li>All settings configurable directly through BepInEx menu</li>\n</ul></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-2\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Installation</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p>Unpack the zip and drop the user folder into your SPTarkov root.</p>\n<p>(Use 7Zip <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.7-zip.org/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Here</a>)</p>\n<p>Install demo video (credit to Drakia):</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/vKRw58b.gif\" alt=\"Demonstration\" /></p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-3\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Known Issues</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p>None that I know of.<br />\nDoes not work with Fika Headless.</p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-4\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">Credits</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Drakia</strong> for: The install video</p></div></div>\n<div id=\"tabset-1-panel-5\" class=\"tab-panel\"><div class=\"tab-title\">What is Dragon Den</div>\n<div class=\"tab-content\"><p><strong>Dragon Den</strong> is my twist on Tarkov. It’s where cuteness, edgyness, and weirdness all collide, while still keeping things believable.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Traders with their own quirks and attitude</li>\n<li>Custom items and quests that feel fresh</li>\n<li>Backpacks, armor, facewear and headwear with personality</li>\n<li>Odd creations that shouldn’t exist… but somehow fit right in</li>\n</ul>\n<p>No weapons, just everything else that makes Tarkov less boring.</p>\n<p>Want to reach me? Look for #drexiras-dragon-den in <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://discord.gg/WelcomeToTarkov\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Welcome To Tarkov’s Discord</a></p></div></div></div>\n<div class=\"youtube-lite\" data-video-id=\"jFKQn02TFjE\" data-embed-url=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/jFKQn02TFjE?autoplay=1\"><img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/jFKQn02TFjE/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"YouTube video thumbnail\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" /></div>\n",
